@Appearance mapping
This screen allows editing the appearance mapping array. Some
element definitions will refer to these, for the following purposes:

þ Line joining
þ Animations
þ Custom parameter mapping

They are not needed for all kinds of appearances of elements; specifically,
it is never needed where the parameter of a tile controls the character
directly or when an element uses a fixed character for its appearance.
Note that "custom parameter mapping" includes cases where only a part of
the parameter controls the appearance rather than all of it; for example
if the low 2-bits specify a direction.

Most uses will require a range of contiguous appearance mappings. Some uses
will require the starting offset to be a multiple of 2, 4, or 16; see the
documentation about element definitions for details about this.

